{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794485306,"nonce":"yylrpyBSbLn34qhHw2zOl3vkiyc=","message":"Committed as eca5429. (1) A Rust static library does not carry the system libraries it links to an hxcpp program's link, so -lsqlite3 was missing for an imported sqlite3 and the link failed; the build now runs cargo with --message-format=json-render-diagnostics, reads each build script's linked_libs and linked_paths (static libraries left out: they are in the archive), and writes link.xml beside the archive. The generated glue includes it under \u003cLIB\u003e_LINK, which hxn build and hxn.Bind define, and hxn package copies it into native/\u003ctriple\u003e/. This applies to any library whose crates link a system library. (2) hxcpp recompiles a file only when the file is newer than its object, so after the symbol rename it linked objects inlined from the old glue (counter gen-cpp, gen-cppia, gen-emcc and the examples failed on reused output directories; fresh ones passed). The generated build XML now lists hxn.h and the library's two headers as \u003cdepend\u003es. Rerun on the same directories: all pass.","files":null}]}